 past sell-offs it fell 54% in the 2020 crash, 28% in the 2022 bear market and 75% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 58% below its blended-model fair value of $416, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 59%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 8.4 vs 17.7 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 130% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -3.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 7.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 12 covering analysts target $214 on average, 22% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 7.1% by 15pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.42).","It runs a 17% gross margin and burns cash (FCF margin -1%).","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only 0.17x.","ROE of 28% is amplified by 6.1x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.1x net debt to EBITDA ($58.6M of cash against $3.9B of debt), with interest covered 6.9x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.0, in the safe zone).","The current ratio of 0.84 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","The Beneish M-score (-2.22) sits just under the manipulation line, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.8% over 3 years, 6.3% over 5 years and 2.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00, a backlog worth 0% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 3%.","Capex runs 1.8x depreciation (1.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.5%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 10 purchases and 2 sales over the past year, net $1.0M bought.","It returns 14.1% a year to shareholders (14.1% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 12.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 13.8% of the float, 4.7 days to cover."],"people":["With about 24,800 employees, each generates about $1.1M of revenue, 2.9x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 5.5% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$8K per employee.","CEO pay is $6.3M (6x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":72,"head":"Invest: trades 58% below fair value of $416; ROIC 22.0% vs WACC 7.1%.","pros":["Composite 46, above the 39 line (gates 13/25)","Trades 58% below fair value of $416","ROIC 22.0% vs WACC 7.1%","Altman Z in the safe zone","P/E 8.4x vs sector 17.7x"],"cons":["FCF margin 0.7% (burns cash)","Net debt/EBITDA 3.1x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":353.33,"vc":{"base":415.68,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":415.68,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.5856,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (59% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":17.7245,"ev_ebitda":10.514,"pfcf":15.7535,"pb":2.1712,"roic":0.127,"gross_margin":0.3467,"fcf_margin":0.0625,"div_yield":0.0235}},"ticker":"AN","date":"2026-11-20"}